{"title":"46","section":"103","heading":"Boundary Line","lead":"In this title, the term “Boundary Line” means a line established under section 2(b) of the Act of February 19, 1895 (33 U.S.C. 151(b)).","tree":[],"notes":[{"topic":"historicalAndRevision","heading":"","text":"Historical and Revision Notes RevisedSectionSource (U.S. Code)Source (Statutes at Large) 10346:2101(3)."},{"topic":"amendments","heading":"Amendments","text":"2016—Pub. L. 114–120 substituted “(33 U.S.C. 151(b)).” for “(33 U.S.C. 151).”"}],"sourceCredit":"(Pub. L. 109–304, § 4, Oct. 6, 2006, 120 Stat. 1486; Pub. L. 114–120, title III, § 306(a)(1), Feb. 8, 2016, 130 Stat. 54.)","releasePoint":"119-102","ancestors":[{"type":"title","num":"Title 46—","heading":"SHIPPING","identifier":"/us/usc/t46"},{"type":"subtitle","num":"Subtitle I—","heading":"General","identifier":"/us/usc/t46/stI"},{"type":"chapter","num":"CHAPTER 1—","heading":"DEFINITIONS","identifier":"/us/usc/t46/stI/ch1"}]}